  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SITE FREE network (2014-2019) FROGEE (2019-2021) - SITE FREE network (2014-2019) FROGEE (2019-2021) Regional</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SITE FREE network (2014-2019) FROGEE (2019-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SITE Network of economic research on transition economis. There is a separate decision for Russian part.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SITE har ett m&#xe5;ng&#xe5;rigt forskningssamarbete med systerorganisationer i regionen. Insatsen syftar till att tillg&#xe4;ngligg&#xf6;ra resultaten f&#xf6;r beslutsfattare och civila samh&#xe4;llet. SITE vill d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r
- etablera en plattform f&#xf6;r att kunna sprida befintlig kunskap
- verka f&#xf6;r bibeh&#xe5;llen j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet inom forskargruppen
- &#xf6;ka forskningsutbyte och samverkan internationellt
- ge administrativt st&#xf6;d till institutionerna f&#xf6;r en mer aktiv roll

Insatsen f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas bidra till att beslutsfattare b&#xe4;ttre kan formulera reformf&#xf6;rslag utifr&#xe5;n sin egen verklighet och ha b&#xe4;ttre m&#xf6;jlighet att f&#xf6;rankara reformerna hos allm&#xe4;nheten. Reformerna &#xe4;r n&#xf6;dv&#xe4;ndiga f&#xf6;r utvecklingen mot marknadsekonomi. Kunskap och f&#xf6;rankring &#xe4;r n&#xf6;dv&#xe4;ndiga f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad stabilitet och en f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttning f&#xf6;r ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The project &quot;Extending the FREE network project: Forum for Research on Gender gaps Eastern Europe (FROGEE) 2014 - 2021&quot;  Contribution No. 55030237 is implemented within the FREE (Forum for Research on Eastern Europe and emerging economies) and is led by Stockholm institute of transitions economy. The initiative includes institutions in Russia (CEFIR and NES), Latvia (BICEPS and SSE Riga), Poland (CenEA), Belarus (BEROC), Ukraine (KSE), and Georgia (ISET). with the aim to build these institutions, the ambition has been to attract WesternThe overall objective of the project is to enable reforms that contribute to economic development and EU integration, by way of strengthening economics education, research and policy advice in all Eastern Partnership countries.

The project has 4 main objective areas: 
I) Increase impact of Policy Analysis, the FREE and FROGEE Policy Briefs, and other activities to support the reform process
II) Women and men shall have the same possibility to conduct qualified
research
III) Enhance Research Exchange and Collaboration
IV) Support Local Capacity Building

Sub-goals o the project is:
- An established platform to be able to disseminate existing knowledge
-Maintained gender equality within the research group
- Increased research exchange and collaboration
better functioning research institutions with increased administrative support</narrative>
  </description>
